menu "Micro OS drivers"

config MICRO_OS_MIC
    bool "SPM1423 microphone on I2S (PDM)"
    default y
    help
      The microphone of the StickC Plus2: an SPM1423 MEMS element with a
      PDM output, clocked on G0 and sampled on G34 by the I2S peripheral.
      The hardware doctor listens to a short window at every boot and
      reports the level it hears, and the shell command "mic" shows the
      level of one window. Turning this off gives the I2S channel and its
      DMA buffers back to an application that needs them.

config MICRO_OS_BUZZER_BEEP_ON_CHECK
    bool "Beep at boot to prove that the buzzer works"
    default n
    help
      The hardware doctor sounds the buzzer for 30 ms at every boot,
      so that the buzzer and its LEDC timer can be heard working.
      The check itself does not need the sound - the state of the
      module is the same either way - so the beep is off by default
      and this switch brings it back.

endmenu
